    "title": "What time is Yankees vs Giants game? How to watch MLB Opening Day on Netflix",
    "text": "Updated March 25, 2026, 8:44 p.m. ETThe 2026 Major League Baseball season begins on Wednesday with a matchup between the New York Yankees and San Francisco Giants at Oracle Park – the first game to be broadcast exclusively on Netflix.Three-time MVP Aaron Judge leads the Yankees into the new campaign, hoping to snap the Bombers' 17-year World Series championship drought. Judge won his first batting title last season but New York fell to the eventual AL champion Toronto Blue Jays in the American League Division Series.\"October is a long way away,” Yankees manager Aaron Boone told reporters Tuesday. “Obviously, we want to get there and play in it and be the last team, but there’s just so many things you got to go through as a team to give yourself a chance to be in that position.\" Get Yankees-Giants opening day tickets!Meanwhile, it's a new era in San Francisco with rookie manager Tony Vitello taking over for the Giants. The team hasn't made the playoffs – or finished with a winning record – since 2021.The opener is a battle of aces with Max Fried taking the mound for the Yankees and Logan Webb getting the Game 1 nod for the Giants.Here's what to know for MLB's opening night:What time is Yankees vs Giants game tonight?First pitch at Oracle Park is scheduled for 8 p.m. ET on Wednesday, March 25.How to watch Yankees vs Giants on NetflixWednesday's season-opening Yankees-Giants game will air exclusively on Netflix and can be watched live with a subscription.This marks Netflix's first endeavor streaming a Major League Baseball game, and the service also has exclusive rights to July's Home Run Derby and August's \"Field of Dreams\" game.Yankees and Giants opening day starting pitchersYankees: LHP Max Fried – 19-5, 2.86 ERA in 2025Giants: RHP Logan Webb – 15-11, 3.22 ERAMLB Opening Day ticketsBuy tickets for every MLB team!Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
